## 12. Tunable Parameters — Summary

| Parameter                       | Starting value | Where |
|---------------------------------|----------------|-------|
| Confidence threshold            | 0.50           | §3 |
| `err_x` aligned band            | `|err| < 0.10` | §4.1 |
| Full-gate aspect threshold      | `aspect > 1.3` | §4.2 |
| Single-bar aspect threshold     | `aspect < 0.5` | §4.2 |
| Pass-through fill threshold     | `fill ≥ 0.60`  | §4.3 |
| Overshoot fill threshold        | `fill ≥ 0.25` (single bar) | §6 |
| EMA alpha for `err_x`           | 0.30           | §8 |
| FSM hysteresis frames           | 3–5            | §8 |
| SEARCHING trigger (missed frames) | 10           | §7 |

All values assume a ~17 FPS stream; scale frame counts proportionally for other frame rates.

---

## 13. Known Limitations

- **Monocular range estimation** via `fill` is coarse. If gate dimensions are known, a PnP-based distance estimate using the four corner keypoints would be more accurate — consider swapping YOLOv26n-det for a keypoint variant once the basic loop works.
- **Single-class detector** forces geometric inference for left/right bars, which is fragile. Retraining with three classes is strongly recommended.
- **Turbidity / lighting changes** will push detector confidence down; the `SEARCHING` fallback handles this gracefully but very low visibility (`conf < 0.3` consistently) needs a different strategy (e.g. sonar or acoustic beacon).
- **Surface reflections** visible in the sample frame can be misread by the detector as gate-like structures. Train with negative examples that include ripples and tiled pool walls.

